// Unit types. Speed is in blocks per second, hp is hit points, trainTime is in seconds and cost is in
// goods (food, wood, stone, iron_ore, coal, iron). trainedAt names the building that trains the unit;
// requires names a tech the player must have researched first; faction (optional) limits the unit to
// one faction. Roles: worker, line_infantry, heavy_infantry, ranged, cavalry, sapper, caster, siege, monster,
// trader (see roles.json for what each is strong and weak against). description (optional) is shown in the game.
// batch (optional, default 1): how many hatch from one training, all for its cost and trainTime, once there is housing
// for all of them (the Deepfolk's swarms). burst (optional, percent): for a few seconds after the unit comes up out
// of the ground (from under natural ground over its head; see Fog of war in docs/rules.md) its blows deal that many
// percent more damage (see CombatSystem.BurstSeconds).
// Combat: damage is the hit points one hit takes off (a unit without damage cannot attack), attackTime
// the seconds between hits, range how far it hits (in blocks, from the middle of the unit; more than 2
// makes it a ranged unit), sight how far it spots enemies to fight on its own, and splash (optional)
// hits every enemy that close to the target too. blast (optional; siege, boulders, strong magic) deals full
// damage to a thick wall, gate or tower (see buildings.json) and topples what stands above and beside a block
// it knocks out of one, away from the blast, onto whoever is behind. weakTo (optional) lists roles whose attacks deal it
// that many percent more damage, as in { "caster": 50 }. heal (optional) is the hit points it gives back
// to the most hurt ally within healRange blocks every healTime seconds. earthWall, iceBridge, chasm and growForest (optional) let it cast
// Earth Wall, Ice Bridge, Chasm and Grow Forest (see Terrain magic in docs/rules.md); flood (optional) lets it cast Flood.
// amphibious (optional): it wades as fast as it walks, mud does not slow it, its regen doubles with its feet in water,
// and lying in the water with nothing to fight it is hidden until an enemy comes close (the Reptilians).
// coldBlooded (optional): at night and up in the hills it walks and strikes a quarter slower and softer, and its regen
// stops (the Reptilians; see "The Reptilians" in docs/rules.md).
// camouflage (optional): standing still with nothing to fight it is hidden until an enemy comes close, and lies in wait
// (Clan Kage). shadowborn (optional): out in the daylight it strikes a fifth softer, and in the shadowed wilds a quarter
// harder. assassin (optional): that many percent more damage to workers, casters and heroes (see "Clan Kage" in docs/rules.md).
// darkSight (optional): night, weather and mist do not shorten its sight, and underground it sees twice as far.
// hearing (optional): columns round it in which it hears units underground, as a listening post does. caveWise
// (optional): lava's heat does not hurt it, and in the deep caves wild monsters do not go after it (the delver).
// Armour (see Combat in docs/rules.md): attack (optional, default slash) is the kind of the unit's attack:
// slash (swords, axes, claws), pierce (spears, arrows, lances) or crush (hammers, clubs, stones, blasts).
// Armour stops slash best and crush least, and slash and pierce wounds bleed. body (optional) is humanoid
// (head, torso, arms, legs; the default) or beast (head, body, legs). armor (optional) is the armour on
// each part, as in { "head": 1, "torso": 2, "arms": 1, "legs": 1 } (a beast's: head, body, legs); each hit
// on a part loses that many points, more against slash and fewer against crush. shield (optional) is the
// percent chance a hit from in front of the unit is stopped whole. bleeds (optional, default true) says
// whether its slash and pierce wounds bleed (see "bleeding" in roles.json); set it false for a body with no
// blood in it.
// start (optional, default true): false keeps a trained unit out of the units matches start with, so it is
// only ever trained (the healer).
// work (optional, default 100) is how fast it gathers, builds, farms and digs tunnels, in percent. regen
// (optional, default 0) is the percent of its
// hit points it heals each second even in a fight (the ogres); out of the fight it heals at this rate or the
// usual one, whichever is faster. nightRegen (optional, default false): its regen works only out of the daylight (the
// trolls): by night, at dawn and dusk, and under rock or a roof, but not under the open sky by day.
// Evolution: a unit with evolvesFrom is a form that unit can take once it has the experience (see
// "experience" in factions.json): it is not trained, and a form of a form needs one level more. Most
// forms simply grow stronger; some give something and take something: less speed or a weakness (weakTo).
// A form with fromDen (optional) is not reached through experience: a unit takes it
// only at a cleared monster den, for a faction whose prize there names it ("prizes" in a lair, below).
// hero (optional): the unit is one of a kind: a player has at most one living, none of theirs evolves into
// it while one lives, and it never breaks and runs. rally (optional, blocks): its own side's units within
// that distance (itself included) are steadied: they lose steady percent less morale to deaths near them,
// and get inspire morale back a second instead of 1 (see Morale in docs/rules.md); the ranged ones among them
// deal volley percent more damage, the cavalry among them move spur percent faster, and the sappers among them
// work undermine percent faster: their blows on buildings land that much harder and they dig that much faster;
// a spell cast by a caster among them is ready again quicken percent sooner (100 halves the wait), and the
// workers among them work hasten percent faster: they gather, build, farm, quarry, dig and clean that much faster.
// drums (optional, needs rally; the war drummer): its own side's broken units within its rally range (its earshot)
// run to it instead of home and rally there, and it can beat the charge: for time seconds its side's units in earshot
// walk speed percent faster and the first blow each strikes deals blow percent more; then it waits wait seconds
// (from the start of the charge) before the next. While it drums, rivals with anything within heard columns see it
// through the fog of war.
// pen (optional, a monster): a tamed beast its owner can keep in a beast pen and loose from it as a stampede (see the
// pen in buildings.json).
// web (optional; the giant spider): { pace, time }: each of its blows that lands (not on a shield, not a splash) wraps
// the unit struck in silk, so it walks at pace percent of its pace for time seconds. Ships and machines are not webbed.
// Monsters: a unit with lair (role monster) lives in the wild, in packs that guard their dens. Each match
// has a lair for every start, on the way to the map centre. pack is the monsters in a lair, guard how
// near its den (blocks) the pack goes after other players' units, leash how far from the den a monster
// chases before it goes back, and reward the goods a player gets for clearing the lair, unless their
// faction tames monsters (see "tamesMonsters" in factions.json): then each monster their units beat is
// theirs to ride or to recruit. A lair with duskTree guards the map's one dusk tree instead (see "Dusk tree" in
// docs/rules.md): it is not placed at the starts and leaves no den.
// biome and count (optional) spread count lairs of the monster over that biome (grassland, forest, hills,
// swamp, beach or wilds, the shadowed wilds round the middle of the map) for each 512 by 512 blocks of map,
// well away from the starts, the towns and each other; such a monster has no lair at the starts unless
// atStarts is true. grow (optional, seconds) makes the pack grow the longer it is left: every grow seconds
// while the lair stands, one more of the monster is born at its den, until the pack is growTo strong
// (twice pack if left out). lurk (optional) has the pack wait in the shallow water by its den, one monster to
// a pool column, unseen while it lies there until another player's unit comes within 3 columns (with fog of
// war on); ambush (optional, percent, needs lurk) is how much harder the first blow is that a monster strikes
// coming up out of the water. pass (optional, needs biome) puts a lair in the middle of each of the map's
// mountain passes, the gaps through the stone ridges across the hill ranges, instead of spreading count over
// the biome (which it falls back to on a map with no pass). spread (optional, seconds, needs biome) has the packs
// spread across the map found new lairs: every spread seconds (the first time after twice that) a lair whose pack is at full strength and not
// fighting has a new pack born at its den, which goes off to a new den of its own in the same biome, up to
// spreadTo lairs of the monster standing for each 512 by 512 blocks of map (twice count if left out).
// prizes (optional): what each faction gets for beating the monster, by faction id. A cleared lair leaves
// a den that one player of a faction with a prize can use, once: { "building": id } puts that building (one
// with "fromDen" in buildings.json) up on the den as a site to build, { "form": id } has the nearest unit
// near the den that can take that form (one with "fromDen") take it, and { "relic": id } has the nearest
// fighting unit near it without a relic take up that relic (relics.json). Two factions can share a prize.
// Without prizes, a cleared lair leaves no den.
// ride (optional) says which unit can climb on a beaten monster (rider) and what it becomes (becomes); a
// recruited monster fights for its new owner as it is. tracksBlood (optional)
// makes a wild monster follow a fresh blood trail it finds to the bleeding unit, well past its leash.
// Siege engines: minRange (optional, blocks) is how near an enemy unit can be and still be hit (a catapult's dead
// ground: anything closer is safe from it; buildings are hit at any distance), lobs (optional) sends its shots up in
// a high arc, so it needs no clear line and hits what stands behind walls and hills, and machine (optional) marks a
// machine that never breaks and runs and does not bleed. ram (optional) makes it a ram: it attacks buildings only,
// never units (not even when ordered to), striking a column's bottom block so the rest falls, as a sapper does;
// gates (optional, percent, default 100) is what its blows on a gate deal next to any other building. cover
// (optional, percent) is how much less arrows and other ranged piercing shots hurt it (a roof over it).
// catch (optional, boats only, instead of seats) makes a boat a fishing boat: out on open water it fishes for fishTime
// seconds (default 20) and brings catch food home to its dock, again and again (see "Fishing boats" in docs/rules.md).
// sails (optional) makes a unit of a role other than boat a ship: it sails on open water as a boat does (built at a
// dock, launched onto the water beside it) but carries nobody; a ship that fights sails within range of its target.
// crater (optional, blocks, needs
// blast and range) is how far round where its shots land they blow a crater in the open ground, throwing the earth
// out onto the rim.
// City-states (see citystates.json): a unit with the trader role is a caravan, which trades with a
// city-state's town; caravans are trained but no player starts with one. A unit with hiredFrom is a
// mercenary: not trained, but hired for its cost at that city-state's town by the city-state's ally.
